1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Hell Pass!

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:04,020
Dream safe!

3
00:00:13,913 --> 00:00:15,560
There's one and the
�ally wind along the sea,

4
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:18,077
and that's what kind of places are they.

5
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,042
But there is nothing and
there's one thing to do.

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,540
But let's unleash the
storytelling back and roll!

7
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,240
Bunchy-bunchy know-do-meat!

8
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,220
Here comes the one piece!

9
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:35,760
All of us are beyond the boat,
that's the ambition of my world.

10
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:45,220
Thank you.

11
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:35,520
All of you need to run.

12
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,140
Evacuate the island!

13
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,275
What are you talking about, Sentomaru?

14
00:01:41,420 --> 00:01:43,244
Do you know something we don't?

15
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,400
What's going to happen to Egghead?

16
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,000
What's going on here?

17
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,160
Why did you deploy the pacifistas?

18
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:54,960
Years ago, there was a place called Ohara,

19
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:58,672
an island of scholars that
disappeared one day, wiped out.

20
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:05,476
They called them fanatics,
traitors to the government.

21
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,880
And their punishment was death.

22
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:17,500
The island of Ohara was once home to
the greatest library in the world.

23
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,837
Its scholars attempted to
decipher the polyglyphs,

24
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:23,017
taking a glimpse into forbidden history,

25
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:25,512
and the government's judgment was fierce.

26
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,620
They instituted a Buster Call,

27
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:31,157
leveling the island to the
ground in a massive bombardment.

28
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:37,460
Barnett, the destruction was so vast that
only one young girl survived, Nico Robin.

29
00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,657
Hunk has the greatest
mind in the whole world,

30
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,477
and the world government still chose
to put him in their crosshairs.

31
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:49,280
Over and over, they've
made one thing clear.

32
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,220
They will kill anyone
to bury their secrets.

33
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:02,961
If you don't escape, you'll end up
just like the scholars of Ohara.

34
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:06,668
This island may be doomed, but
you don't have to die with it.

35
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:17,300
Come on, Straw Hat, hurry up!

36
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,640
We don't have a moment to lose.

37
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:39,020
Hey!

38
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,120
And pistols!

39
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:06,600
Dumb, dumb!

40
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,070
Yellow lotus!

41
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,760
Call Morgan gun!

42
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:26,080
It's the best kick!

43
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,480
Slaughter!

44
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,840
White Thunder!

45
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,760
One sword's dire, the eye!

46
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,380
Death, lion's sword!

47
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:55,050
Aaaaaaah!

48
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,360
Aaaaaaah!

49
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:22,930
Ahh!

50
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,080
Wait, they're getting
up already? What gives?

51
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,997
How many comebacks are you going to have?

52
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,280
Who are you, Kaido?

53
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:37,297
Our attacks are hitting, but
they're not doing anything.

54
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:41,086
Now that I look, they kind of
remind me of this guy named King.

55
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:44,340
He and I had a pretty
serious fight back in Wano.

56
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:48,517
Are you saying there was a
Lunarian in Kaido's crew?

57
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:51,680
I wouldn't know, but
he had fire and wings.

58
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:53,170
I see.

59
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:56,837
Years ago, there was a
Lunarian held at Punk Hazard.

60
00:05:56,920 --> 00:06:00,214
He was used as a guinea pig
until he escaped with Kaido.

61
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,540
His name was Alvair.

62
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:04,831
Thanks to him, we acquired Lunarian blood.

63
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:08,240
And the Seraphim were
indeed augmented with it.

64
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,174
Alright, good to know.

65
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:11,530
Listen, guys.

66
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,137
You gotta watch the flames
on their back real close.

67
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,050
It's tricky.

68
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:17,437
Wait till the fire goes out for a sec.

69
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,937
That's the only time
your attacks will work.

70
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:22,902
They're pretty much
invincible when it's burning.

71
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:28,258
Guess I made you waste your stamina.

72
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,777
Honestly, I probably should
have noticed that right away.

73
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,978
At least we found out in time to win

74
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:40,460
They do look like King same
white hair same brown skin.

75
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:42,700
Same black wings.

76
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,040
And the big flames too?

77
00:06:54,260 --> 00:06:56,497
Hey helmet guy, where are you going?

78
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,360
to find Stella.

79
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:01,039
There's one more place he could be.

80
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:08,360
Then go!

81
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:09,850
All right.

82
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,200
Thank you.

83
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:15,660
We've got places to be, so
don't get in our way. Got it?

84
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:27,500
Let's do this, Zeus! Yeah!

85
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,280
That's right!

86
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:30,500
He's no child!

87
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:33,920
He tried to murder my friends!

88
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,920
He have destroyed Edison!

89
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:37,880
He's a killing machine!

90
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,897
He's not cheap, and he's not cute at all!

91
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:45,720
We got this, Nami.

92
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:46,920
Don't hesitate.

93
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,620
I'll take care of him.

94
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,180
Just let me rip.

95
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:53,340
Keep your eyes closed
if you have to. My feet!

96
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,220
It's not enough.

97
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,080
Then here's some more!

98
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:14,100
I got you!

99
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,660
Sorry, little Jinbei.

100
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,760
Oh, no.

101
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:27,157
He's gone down again!

102
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,220
Run for it!

103
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:31,057
Watch out!

104
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,420
It's coming from the home! What?

105
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,520
But I beat him, didn't I?

106
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,660
The Sanji Constitution, Article 1.

107
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:56,677
The punishment for
upsetting Nami is death.

108
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,180
Ahhhh!

109
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,680
Agh!

110
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,340
Baaaaaaarghh? Huh?

111
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:06,160
The Sanji Constitution, Article 9.

112
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:10,500
The punishment for making
Nami's stream is this!

113
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,420
Pawheat Strike!

114
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:25,817
Sanji!

115
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,760
You okay, Nami? You hurt?

116
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,440
I'm fine, thanks.

117
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,132
That's all that matters.

118
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,140
Let me take care of the rest.

119
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,217
That was your warning, brat!

120
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:37,241
Now you're dead!

121
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:46,740
Nami showed mercy, but I'm not so kind.

122
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:51,340
You're looking at your
executioner, Jinbei Jr.

123
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:58,037
I can't believe you turned York into
stone, you backstabbing little snot!

124
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:01,577
They're, like, specially engineered
to destroy people, right?

125
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:04,260
My bubble gun can handle this easy.

126
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,710
Really?

127
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:11,480
That didn't work at all!

128
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:21,100
You thought you had me, huh?

129
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,057
The bubbles from this gun
have a secret ingredient.

130
00:10:27,140 --> 00:10:29,677
They're instilled with
the energy of the sea.

131
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,440
And you've got green blood.

132
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,937
Which means you have the same weakness
as people who ate a Devil Fruit.

133
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:37,608
My bubbles aren't so
harmless now, are they?

134
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,670
Yeah!

135
00:10:39,753 --> 00:10:41,280
You are a genius! Nice work!

136
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:43,580
Yeah, obviously. Come on.

137
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:47,797
Franky, restrain her while
we still have the chance.

138
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,020
You got it, bro.

139
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:57,980
Don't touch me!

140
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,860
You insolent boar.

141
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:05,280
Bow before me!

142
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,797
Looks like your bubble
thing wore off fast.

143
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:09,697
Yeah, that's because the
bubble only grazed her.

144
00:11:09,780 --> 00:11:13,040
It's got a stick for the
effect to last. You stink!

145
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:19,750
Ah!

146
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:20,663
She's angry!

147
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,280
We gotta go!

148
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,857
She's about to shoot a laser!

149
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:25,770
Move!

150
00:11:25,853 --> 00:11:27,700
Okay, let's fuck it!

151
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,780
No, I stink!

152
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,340
Please don't do it!

153
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:35,911
You're gonna get one hell of
a time after this, young lady!

154
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,940
You let your guard down!

155
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:56,960
Nap time!

156
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,635
Now sit your sassy ass down, princess.

157
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,020
You're a genius too, Freaky!

158
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:05,740
I told you!

159
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,100
The bubbles work!

160
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,220
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

161
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,600
Play nice, kid.

162
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:12,700
It's over.

163
00:12:14,020 --> 00:12:15,300
It hurts.

164
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:16,440
I'm dying.

165
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,340
Sorry, sorry! Help!

166
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,720
No, I'm tearing a stone!

167
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,000
She got me!

168
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:33,240
Oh, no! Franky!

169
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:34,700
I'll be next!

170
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,280
We're done for!

171
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,400
Oh, here she comes! Stay back!

172
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:01,380
Her love?

173
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:02,540
Beans!

174
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:09,460
Loose up, Lily!

175
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:28,940
We search for Stella in
every wing of the lab.

176
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:32,377
If he's not in this room, then...

177
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,040
Who are you?

178
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:36,080
Did you do this?

179
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,633
Did you put us in here?

180
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:38,780
It can't be.

181
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,197
You must be the missing
Cipher pole agents.

182
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:42,110
What happened?

183
00:13:42,193 --> 00:13:43,023
Why are you here?

184
00:13:43,106 --> 00:13:44,520
Help us. Please.

185
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:46,677
You have to get us out of here.

186
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,380
We don't want to die.

187
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:49,994
We're going to starve.

188
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:56,910
Stella.

189
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:03,268
Thank goodness you're safe.

190
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,660
Who did this to you?

191
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:08,620
Oh, Shaka.

192
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,137
I'm getting you out of here.

193
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:16,437
I'll unlock the tank.

194
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,350
Just hold on.

195
00:14:17,433 --> 00:14:18,263
Wait.

196
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:19,830
Shaka.

197
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:22,420
Who came here? It's you. What?

198
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,440
What just happened?

199
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:44,140
He's been shot!

200
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:14,160
Let's keep our guard
up, shall we? Yes, sir!

201
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:25,730
What?

202
00:15:25,813 --> 00:15:27,171
Uncle Kiesener is coming?

203
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:30,020
And soon, he's commanding an entire fleet.

204
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:32,297
They should be closing in
on Egghead as we speak.

205
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,780
with over 100 ships.

206
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:36,001
That's a bit excessive, isn't it?

207
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,697
CP0's mission was to assassinate Dr.

208
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,610
Vegapunk.

209
00:15:39,693 --> 00:15:41,637
After that, we were
told to wait for Kizaru.

210
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:44,457
This is the firmest stance
they could possibly take.

211
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:47,837
If they're sending an admiral, then
they're not taking any chances.

212
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:51,617
Yes, apparently they're taking this
even more seriously than Ohara.

213
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:53,420
But why? Because Dr.

214
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:57,277
Vegapunk did more than just uncover
what Ohara had already researched.

215
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,190
Much more.

216
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:00,065
He expanded on their findings.

217
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,917
Additionally, egghead is
armed with advanced weaponry.

218
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,837
Something that ohara lacked?

219
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,580
You mean the Seraphim
and other pacifistas?

220
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:14,057
That alone is reason enough
to send a massive force.

221
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,477
They would need an admiral.

222
00:16:15,560 --> 00:16:17,957
Contact me as soon as anything happens!

223
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:21,557
All communication devices in
the labophase are inoperative.

224
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,537
Understood.

225
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:23,640
Kaku.

226
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,397
Did you hear that?

227
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:31,480
One look at history will show you
exactly what the Navy has planned.

228
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,200
But that can't be!

229
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:34,897
You really think they'll kill us all?

230
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:36,417
They'll burn Inkhand to the ground?

231
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,330
That's right!

232
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,397
Which means there's no time to feel sorry!

233
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:42,277
You need to get off this
island as quickly as possible!

234
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,190
Hurry!

235
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,160
Lay the ships!

236
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:48,997
Let's just hope we have enough!

237
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:51,080
But the Navy's almost here, right?

238
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:53,024
Sentomaru says there's no time!

239
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:55,700
Usopp, live Earth!

240
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,240
Unpetrify me right now!

241
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:02,999
So what have you got my right side?

242
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,680
My left arm's loaded.

243
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,497
You think I won't mess you up?

244
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:10,180
I have a weapon's left here,
and it's got your name on it.

245
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:11,712
But I'm a nice guy, see?

246
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:14,018
Surrender now, and I'll let you off.

247
00:17:15,260 --> 00:17:16,090
Huh?

248
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:20,060
I was just, uh...

249
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,480
Hey, are you listening?

250
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:26,996
I swear I'll shoot if you don't stop!

251
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:30,120
I just want to know why, S-Snake!

252
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,124
Whose orders are you following?

253
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,635
Why won't you listen to a word we say?

254
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,420
Oh, please, don't!

255
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:39,520
Stop it!

256
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,370
Phythagoras!

257
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:52,580
Hey, wait!

258
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:54,440
Get back here!

259
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,746
I hope everyone else is okay.

260
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:08,517
They're strong, but we've been hearing
an awful lot of explosions and screams.

261
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,357
The Seraphim are running wild out there.

262
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,440
We need to hurry.

263
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,180
It doesn't make sense.

264
00:18:14,380 --> 00:18:17,657
The Seraphim were helping us,
and then they all went crazy.

265
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:21,916
In that case, perhaps they've received
a new command from someone else.

266
00:18:23,100 --> 00:18:25,280
Should we find Mommy? I'm worried.

267
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:26,550
She'll be fine.

268
00:18:26,633 --> 00:18:28,482
I'm sure Sanji heard her scream,

269
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,677
which means he'll come
running straight to her side.

270
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,980
Oh, good point!

271
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,697
Anyone stuck fighting
can't continue the search.

272
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:41,397
But we've been fortunate enough
not to run into any trouble,

273
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:44,617
so our focus should be finding
Vegapunk just as planned.

274
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:45,530
You're right.

275
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,680
Let's get going.

276
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,917
Hold up a second.

277
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,497
There's a room we haven't used
in a while that's sealed off,

278
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:52,462
so it doesn't have a video feed.

279
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:54,337
It doesn't make sense, though.

280
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:56,037
There's not much reason to go there.

281
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:57,200
It's worth a shot.

282
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:01,317
We have no leads, so that's still
better than wandering around blindly.

283
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,920
Show us the way and we'll follow. New bra!

284
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,740
Edison! Wake up!

285
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,920
Edison! I'm leaving.

286
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:24,926
For now, watch over my old bones and I'll
search for Vegapunk in my spirit form.

287
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:33,320
Oh no!

288
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:34,970
Oh no!

289
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,270
Ah!

290
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,470
Ah!

291
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:41,790
Ah!

292
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:50,060
I saved Sanji!

293
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,757
Sorry, kid.

294
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:57,820
This is the power of love.

295
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,500
It can't be beat.

296
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:05,600
Kuma Kuma!

297
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,000
Green Hawk!

298
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:15,540
What a pain.

299
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:17,517
The flames still haven't gone out yet.

300
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:19,659
We're wasting energy fighting back.

301
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:26,520
Hey, while we were talking,
the Hawkeye Kid ran away!

302
00:20:26,780 --> 00:20:28,015
Why would he do that?

303
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,633
Must have changed their target priority.

304
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:33,020
They realize we are holding them up.

305
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:35,455
They'll kill the weaker targets first.

306
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,588
It functions as a
psychological attack, too.

307
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:41,797
If your friends are killed,
then your resolve may crumble.

308
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:43,000
Luffy, don't worry.

309
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,358
I'll hunt him down.

310
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:45,735
All right, good luck.

311
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,940
Ah, crap! Hey, Usopp!

312
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:49,514
Could you go with him?

313
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:52,308
If he's alone, then
he'll get lost for sure.

314
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,285
Why is he so high maintenance?

315
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:56,460
Get back here, Rotonoa!

316
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:58,010
Hey, wait!

317
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,788
Did you just call me Usopp?

318
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,480
This is our fight. Let them go.

319
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:19,957
I'll just keep punching you!

320
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,980
Go, go, Hulk, get me!

321
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:24,640
Come on, fire, go out!

322
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:26,712
Dammit, Straw Hat, wait!

323
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,017
Beat this through!

324
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:31,453
If you could punch the fire
out, we would've won already!

325
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:38,717
These are the events that would
lead to the Egghead incident,

326
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,580
A tale that would shock
the world to its core.

327
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:45,360
But in truth, it all started
three months earlier.

328
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:49,160
Sacred Marie Joie.

329
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:50,560
Three months ago.

330
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,340
I can't hear you.

331
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,790
I'm okay.

332
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:04,050
This is exit.

333
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:06,480
I need to talk to the my rocks.

334
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:08,504
And what do you want from them?

335
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:10,980
I need to talk to the higher-ups.

336
00:22:11,160 --> 00:22:12,631
I said, what do you want?

337
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,620
It's news about Dr. Vegapunk.

338
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:18,320
He's researching the hybrid history.

339
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:37,057
Upon receiving that tip, Cape was dispatched
to Egghead to question Dr. Vegapunk.

340
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:39,200
and attempt to ascertain the truth.

341
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,700
However, they found no evidence.

342
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,299
After completing the investigation,

343
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:49,073
the agents left on their ship but
mysteriously vanished on their way back.

344
00:22:54,660 --> 00:22:57,340
In light of these strange circumstances,

345
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:01,500
first Cape, then Cape were
dispatched to Egghead.

346
00:23:01,640 --> 00:23:06,820
But just like Cape before them, they found
nothing and disappeared without a trace.

347
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:26,657
Later, there was a meeting
between the five elders.

348
00:23:26,740 --> 00:23:31,057
They spoke to an outside figure who's
incriminating evidence would seal Dr.

349
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:32,199
Beckerbunk's fate.

350
00:23:32,860 --> 00:23:34,389
The betrayal was complete.

351
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:39,000
The Five Elders decided that Dr.

352
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:41,280
Vegapunk must be assassinated.

353
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:47,960
Cypherpole Aegis Zero was tasked
with that mission and set sail.

354
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:49,390
However,

355
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:52,137
they feared a deadly
retaliation from Vegapunk,

356
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:55,808
so one of the Five Elders decided
to go to Egghead in person.

357
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:59,360
He chose Admiral Kizaru as his escort.

358
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:07,260
Taking every precaution,

359
00:24:07,460 --> 00:24:11,740
they also requested reinforcements
from a series of Navy outposts.

360
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:17,660
Together, they formed a fleet.

361
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:20,840
It was a deployment
befitting a full-scale war.

362
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:38,500
However, an unexpected
guest showed up first.

363
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:42,800
The newly crowned Emperor
of the Sea, Straw Hat Luffy.

364
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:56,616
Already facing a difficult operation,

365
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,957
the government feared that the Straw Hats?

366
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:01,040
would throw everything into chaos.

367
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:02,377
See this?

368
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:06,284
You give people an inch and they
give you nothing but a headache.

369
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,280
It's thin again!

370
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:18,820
For better or worse, the incident will
come to a conclusion in only a day's time.

371
00:25:20,540 --> 00:25:25,020
But the aftermath may very well
reshape the future of the entire world.

372
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,200
Is this your doing?

373
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:32,720
All this chaos and destruction?

374
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,120
Answer me!

375
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:10,160
Why are you doing this?

376
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,160
Bye, York!

377
00:26:18,940 --> 00:26:20,440
What do you mean, why?

378
00:26:20,820 --> 00:26:23,760
When this is done, I'll
be a celestial dragon.

379
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:27,940
What are you talking about, York?

380
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:30,398
You've been to Marijwa, haven't you?

381
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:33,935
Why would you want to associate
with leashes like them?

382
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:36,520
You sound just like Shaka.

383
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:39,900
Well, before he ate lead.

384
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:45,660
I never understood having so many of us.

385
00:26:47,700 --> 00:26:48,620
Seven Dr.

386
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:50,440
Vegapunks is a bit much.

387
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:54,440
I think one would be plenty.

388
00:27:29,380 --> 00:27:30,780
Oh

389
00:27:51,580 --> 00:27:56,420
All of you, everyone,
I can't wait for you.

390
00:27:59,460 --> 00:28:05,220
Just one moment, I can't wait for you.

391
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:11,640
I'm laughing at the sky,
I'm laughing at you.

392
00:28:12,580 --> 00:28:16,520
I'm going to sing the same song.

393
00:28:28,180 --> 00:28:29,010
Thank

394
00:28:29,093 --> 00:28:29,923
you

395
00:28:30,006 --> 00:28:35,260
so

396
00:28:39,740 --> 00:28:39,851
much for watching.
